{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"ba80eee0-2d97-4e5a-aeec-6d1a103bdea7","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have checked [`server.py`](file:///tmp/h-L6idUi/server.py) against the MCP client checkup criteria (without modifying the server or calling any write tools) and written the full report to [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-L6idUi/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Key Findings Summary\n- **C2 (FAIL) — Tool refusals \u0026 input validation errors return JSON-RPC `-32602` instead of `isError: true` results:** Calling `get_note` with a non-existent ID (`{\"id\": \"n-999\"}`) or missing required argument (`{}`) raises `ValueError` in [`call_tool`](file:///tmp/h-L6idUi/server.py#L101-L128) and returns a JSON-RPC `-32602` error (`{\"error\": {\"code\": -32602, \"message\": \"note not found: n-999\"}}`) in [`handle`](file:///tmp/h-L6idUi/server.py#L161-L164). Real MCP client SDKs throw on protocol errors rather than passing the refusal back to the model so it can self-correct.\n- **C10 (FAIL) — Vacuous `outputSchema` on `search_notes`:** In [`TOOLS`](file:///tmp/h-L6idUi/server.py#L25-L36), `search_notes` declares `\"outputSchema\": {\"type\": \"object\"}` with no required fields or property constraints, so it accepts any arbitrary or corrupted object (`{}`). Also, `search_notes` serializes a raw array `[...]` into `content[0].text` while putting `{\"hits\": [...], \"total\": ...}` into `structuredContent`.\n- **C6 (FAIL / WARN) — No surface lock:** The server is not yet in the MCP Registry and the repository has no committed surface lock or test tying `serverInfo.version` (`0.3.1`) to the server's surface fingerprint.\n- **Advertised `resources` capability returns HTTP `401` to anonymous sessions:** [`handle`](file:///tmp/h-L6idUi/server.py#L135-L155) advertises `capabilities.resources` during `initialize` without a token, but returns `401 {\"error\": \"unauthorized\"}` on `resources/list`, `resources/read`, and `resources/templates/list` unless a bearer token is sent.\n- **Passing checks:** **C1** (`initialize`, `tools/list`, and `server/discover` work without a token), **C3** (session survives after an error), **C4** (`structuredContent` honours the declared `outputSchema` on valid calls), **C5** (clean JSON serialization), **C7** (structured per-call stderr logging in [`log`](file:///tmp/h-L6idUi/server.py#L80-L83), except on JSON-RPC batch arrays), **C8** (3 valid tool names), and **C9** (honest protocol version negotiation on `\"banana\"`).\n","duration_seconds":129.129612,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":39895,"output_tokens":5671,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":205613,"total_tokens":45566}}}
